# Post-Test Cleanup — Phase A: Blockers + routing (CORE, revised)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (locked before implementation)
# A1.1 GIVEN any routed task flow, WHEN its outermost container renders, THEN a
#      persistent top-trailing 44pt X with accessibility id `flow.exit` exists.
#      Nested sheets/covers keep only their native dismissal back to the parent
#      flow and do not render `flow.exit`.
# A1.2 GIVEN no answer has been recorded anywhere in the whole routed flow, WHEN
#      X is tapped, THEN the entire flow and all nested presentation state tear
#      down immediately and the originating tab is restored. A nested surface
#      cannot outlive its parent.
# A1.3 GIVEN at least one answer exists anywhere in the whole flow and the latest
#      answer-persistence write succeeded, WHEN X is tapped, THEN the exact
#      confirmation renders: title `Leave this task?`, body `Your answers are
#      saved. Pick up where you left off anytime.`, buttons `Leave` / `Keep
#      going`. Keep going preserves state; Leave tears down the whole flow and
#      returns to its originating tab.
# A1.4 GIVEN the latest answer-persistence write is pending or failed, WHEN X is
#      tapped, THEN the dialog cannot claim the answer is saved and instead uses
#      the exact body `We couldn't save your last answer — check your connection
#      before leaving.` with buttons `Leave anyway` / `Keep going`. The flow
#      tracks `lastPersistenceError` at flow scope.
# A1.5 GIVEN a successful recorded step, WHEN the flow is left and reopened,
#      THEN resume enters at the outermost saved step with whole-flow answer state
#      restored, including answers contributed by nested layers.
# A1.6 GIVEN the scoped flow answer-persistence paths, WHEN Phase A closes, THEN
#      every encountered `try?` or swallowed `catch` is reported for a future
#      chip. This phase does not perform a global `try?` audit.
# A2.1 GIVEN an unauthenticated device where `peezy.explainer.seen` is false,
#      WHEN AppRootView resolves routing, THEN ExplainerView renders before Auth.
# A2.2 GIVEN explainer card 5, THEN its body exactly matches the sanctioned signup
#      copy; completion retains the device-scoped key and routes to Auth without
#      changing SIWA/AuthViewModel internals.
# A3.1 GIVEN either frozen-dose completion path, including `.allComplete`, WHEN
#      the Home stack renders, THEN no completion card/glass chrome exists. The
#      existing locked `That's today.` / `You're on pace for {moveDate}.` copy is
#      the stack empty state and get-ahead remains visually secondary. The phase
#      report cites the deleted `.allComplete` render path.
# A4.1 GIVEN Tasks contains tasks whose `snoozedUntil` is in the future, WHEN the
#      tab renders, THEN a separate Snoozed section shows every such task and its
#      return date; expired or dateless tasks are not classified as snoozed, and
#      the app retains exactly four tabs.
